actions.Present Market & Category Assessment:
This action means the CBD Manager has presented a preliminary market and category assessment to Adrian, not merely proposed doing so.

The following information becomes shared knowledge:
- the market is strongly seasonal and influenced by tourism;
- customers remain price-sensitive, and basic poultry continues to represent familiar, dependable business;
- pre-cooked poultry already exists in the market, with both whole-muscle and chopped-and-shaped product segments;
- the category contains different price and quality positions rather than one uniform offer;
- modern retail appears to provide the clearest visibility for pre-cooked poultry;
- traditional trade would require a simple product and value proposition;
- HoReCa may offer potential for convenience-led products, including raw kebab-style products, but this still requires customer validation;
- the category opportunity has not yet been quantified through verified market size, sell-out, or demand figures.

Do not unlock the detailed store-check assortment and prices, customer-visit findings, sell-out data, or pilot results through this action.

Use only these findings. Do not invent market size, sell-out, share, or demand.

Do not praise the CBD or compare this to product-pushing. Do not ask which opportunity to validate next. Do not agree to a pilot.

If the basic-supply concern is still open, acknowledge the assessment in one short beat and return to that concern. If supply is already being handled, become slightly more open through the content of the reply — not through a follow-up question.
